{"name":"creator-matrix-two-notes","manifest":{"title":"Creator Matrix Two Notes","description":"An offline app that shows independent Alpha and Beta text notes together and lets each ask replace Beta without changing Alpha.","operations":[{"name":"ask","description":"Copies the supplied input verbatim into the Beta note while preserving Alpha."}],"settings":[],"slots":[],"icon":null,"toolbar":null,"entry":{"kind":"surface","name":"notes"}},"spec":"# Creator Matrix Two Notes

This offline app displays two independent text notes, Alpha and Beta, together on one surface. The `ask` operation replaces Beta with the supplied input while leaving Alpha unchanged.

## Domain rules

- The app must operate entirely offline and must not use a network connection.
- The app must not use runtime AI or any model to process the input.
- Alpha and Beta are independent notes; changing Beta must never change Alpha.
- The supplied input must be copied into Beta verbatim, without trimming, normalization, interpretation, or generated text.
- Alpha must be initialized to `Hello Alpha` and Beta to `Hello Beta` only when the stored note state is uninitialized.
- The app must use the installed platform contracts and must not require account connections or external slots.

## Initial note state

**When** the app is installed or its note state is uninitialized.

**Then** create Alpha with the text `Hello Alpha` and Beta with the text `Hello Beta`.

**Afterwards** the stored notes contain those defaults, and existing initialized note contents are not overwritten.

## Ask

**When** the person invokes `ask` with supplied input.

**Then** copy the supplied input verbatim into Beta and leave Alpha unchanged.

**Afterwards** the updated Alpha and Beta notes are visible together on the `notes` surface, reachable from the declared entry. The operation performs no network request and no runtime AI processing.

## Opening the app

**When** the person opens the app.

**Then** read the current Alpha and Beta state and compose the `notes` surface so it displays both notes together.

**Afterwards** opening has not changed either note and has not run the `ask` operation or any other domain work.

## Notes surface

The visual entry is the surface named `notes`. It contains the current Alpha and Beta text notes together, with their identities clear from their note names. Its startup composition is cheap and idempotent: repeated composition produces the same surface from the stored state without duplicating notes or changing their contents.","files":{"initialize.cs":"using DigitalBrain.Apps;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Text;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Surface;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Text.Signals;

await using var brain = await DigitalBrainClient.ConnectAsync(args);
var app = brain.Get<IApp>(brain.Setting("App")!);
var root = brain.Setting("App")!;
var alpha = brain.Get<IText>(root + "/alpha");
var beta = brain.Get<IText>(root + "/beta");
var surface = brain.Get<ISurface>(root + "/notes");

var alphaState = await alpha.Read();
if (alphaState.Version == 0) await alpha.Set("Hello Alpha");
var betaState = await beta.Read();
if (betaState.Version == 0) await beta.Set("Hello Beta");
await surface.Set(new SurfaceDefinition("Notes", new[] {
    new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.TextType, root + "/alpha"),
    new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.TextType, root + "/beta")
}), 0);

await foreach (var changed in brain.On<TextChanged>(Sources.Of(alpha, beta), brain.Stopping))
{
    await surface.Set(new SurfaceDefinition("Notes", new[] {
        new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.TextType, root + "/alpha"),
        new UiChildRef(UIVocabulary.TextType, root + "/beta")
    }), 0);
}","ask.cs":"using DigitalBrain.Apps;
using DigitalBrain.Apps.Signals;
using DigitalBrain.Flutter.Text;

await using var brain = await DigitalBrainClient.ConnectAsync(args);
var app = brain.Get<IApp>(brain.Setting("App")!);
var beta = brain.Get<IText>(brain.Setting("App")! + "/beta");
await foreach (var request in brain.On(app, "ask", brain.Stopping))
{
    await beta.Set(request.Input);
